# The bundle ships the built server only: dist/, production node_modules,
# manifest.json, README.md and LICENSE. Everything below is source, tooling or
# generated reports that a client does not need to run the server.
#
# Anchor any pattern whose name also appears under dist/. These are
# gitignore-style patterns, so an unanchored `view/` matches at every depth and
# silently drops `dist/view/canvas.html` - the MCP Apps resource the server
# reads at resources/read time, which makes the installed bundle broken rather
# than merely smaller. `/view/` matches the source directory only.
# `src/`, `tests/`, `coverage/`, `reports/` have no dist/ counterpart (tsc
# flattens src/ into dist/ and the compiled tests are excluded by name below),
# so they are safe unanchored - anchored anyway, to keep the rule one rule.
/src/
/view/
/tests/
/coverage/
/reports/
/.github/
/.assess/
/.claude/
/.stryker-tmp/
/scripts/
tsconfig.json
eslint.config.js
stryker.config.json
CLAUDE.md
.gitignore
.git/
*.mcpb
dist/*.test.js
dist/e2e.js
# The second, Node-targeted compile of the view's pure modules, built by
# `npm test` only so those tests can run outside the browser. The bundle needs
# dist/view/canvas.html, not this.
/dist/view-test/
